# OPL-1.3 NOTICE File Example
# ============================
#
# This is an EXAMPLE of a NOTICE file for a project licensed under the
# Open-Pact License v1.3 (OPL-1.3). It is a template.
#
# How to use this file:
#   1. Copy this file to NOTICE in the root of your project repository.
#   2. Replace the placeholder values with your real values.
#   3. Remove every line that begins with "#" (these are comments).
#   4. Keep every line that does NOT begin with "#".
#   5. Optional fields may be removed entirely; do not include them at all.
#
# Per OPL-1.3 §13, your NOTICE must include at minimum:
#   - OPL Version
#   - Maintainer's name and reachable contact
#   - Governing Jurisdiction
#   - Standard Terms URL (your published commercial-use pricing/payment terms)
#   - OPL-AI opt-in/opt-out
#
# The following are optional:
#   - Abandonment period (12-60 months; default 36)
#   - Trademark notice
#
# IMPORTANT: If you do not declare a Valid Standard Terms URL, Commercial
# Use is not permitted under LICENSE.md §3.3. A Valid URL is HTTPS, returns
# 2xx, is HTML (not PDF), and is human-readable in a major browser without
# authentication. See LICENSE.md §3.3 for full requirements.
#
# For the full OPL-1.3 license text, see LICENSE.md.
# For the OPL-AI addendum, see OPL-AI-v1.3.md.
# For the Standard Terms requirements, see LICENSE.md §3.3.

# ----- REQUIRED FIELDS -----

OPL Version: 1.3
# The Open-Pact License version this NOTICE is authored against. Useful
# for future-proofing: if you upgrade later, update this line. The
# SPDX-License-Identifier in each source file is the authoritative
# version reference; this line is for human readability.

Maintainer: Your Name <[email protected]>
# A reachable contact. The Maintainer must respond to written licensing
# inquiries within 60 days (LICENSE.md §4.2). Failure to do so for 36
# consecutive months (or whatever period you declare below) triggers
# abandonment per LICENSE.md §5.

Governing Jurisdiction: California, United States
# Use a specific legal jurisdiction: state/province + country. Examples:
# "Delaware, United States", "England and Wales", "New South Wales, Australia",
# "Ontario, Canada", "Berlin, Germany". This is the jurisdiction whose
# laws govern the license per LICENSE.md §12. If unspecified, the
# Maintainer's location applies.

Standard Terms URL: https://example.com/standard-terms
# REQUIRED for Commercial Use to be permitted under LICENSE.md §3.3.
# If absent or invalid, Commercial Use is not permitted.
#
# A Valid Standard Terms URL is one that:
#   (a) is HTTPS
#   (b) returns a 2xx response
#   (c) is a webpage (HTML) — not a PDF, plain text, or other document
#   (d) is human-readable in a major browser without authentication
#
# The page must publish your commercial-use pricing and payment
# mechanism. You choose the mechanism — see EXAMPLE STANDARD TERMS URL
# BLOCKS at the bottom of this file for 5 common patterns.
#
# You may change the URL with 90 days' notice for existing commercial
# users. New users are bound by the Standard Terms as they exist at
# the time of access.

OPL-AI: opted out.
# REQUIRED. State whether the OPL-AI addendum applies. Default (if this
# line is omitted): not incorporated, AI training is permitted.
#
# To opt out (matches the default):  "OPL-AI: opted out. AI training is
#              permitted under the same terms as other use." (Or simply
#              omit this line; the default is opt-out.)
# To opt in:  "OPL-AI: opted in. AI training is restricted under the
#              OPL-AI addendum (v1.3)." See OPL-AI-v1.3.md.

# ----- OPTIONAL FIELDS -----
# Uncomment and fill in any of the following. Remove any you do not need.
# A line that begins with "#" is a comment and will be ignored; remove the
# leading "#" to make a line active. To remove an optional field entirely,
# delete the line.

# Abandonment Period: 24
# A number of months between 12 and 60. Default: 36. After this many
# consecutive months of Maintainer unresponsiveness, the Work
# automatically converts to Apache License 2.0 per LICENSE.md §5.
# A shorter period (e.g., 12) means faster conversion; a longer period
# (e.g., 60) means more time to find a successor.

# Trademark Notice: "FooBar" is a trademark of Your Name. See https://example.com/trademark-policy for permitted use.
# Any trademark notice you wish to assert under LICENSE.md §10.

# ----- EXAMPLE STANDARD TERMS URL BLOCKS (delete this entire section when finalizing your NOTICE) -----
#
# Below are 5 example blocks showing what your Standard Terms page might
# contain. These are PATTERNS, not the actual text — you write your own
# Standard Terms and publish them at the URL you declared above.
#
# The 5 patterns:
#
# 1. SMART CONTRACT (cryptocurrency, on-chain payment)
#    URL: https://example.com/standard-terms
#    Body:
#      "Commercial Use of this Work requires payment to the Maintainer
#       via the following smart contract on Ethereum mainnet:
#         Contract: 0x1234...abcd
#         Function: payLicense()
#         Amount:    0.05 ETH per commercial deployment
#       See https://example.com/pay for instructions. The smart contract
#       is the operative payment mechanism; this page is documentation."
#
# 2. STRIPE LINK (fiat, hosted checkout)
#    URL: https://example.com/standard-terms
#    Body:
#      "Commercial Use of this Work requires payment to the Maintainer
#       via Stripe at https://buy.stripe.com/example-link. Pricing tiers:
#         Solo / indie:  $50/month
#         Team:          $200/month
#         Enterprise:    contact us
#       Annual subscriptions receive a 20% discount."
#
# 3. GITHUB SPONSORS (voluntary; not actually a Commercial-Use gate)
#    URL: https://example.com/standard-terms
#    Body:
#      "Commercial Use of this Work is encouraged (but not required) to
#       sponsor the Maintainer at https://github.com/sponsors/yourname
#       at the 'Silver' tier or above. Sponsorship is voluntary; non-
#       sponsorship does not prohibit Commercial Use under this license.
#       (Note: this is a 'voluntary Commercial Use' model — the license
#       permits Commercial Use without payment; sponsorship is at the
#       user's discretion.)"
#
# 4. CONTACT EMAIL (negotiated, no public pricing)
#    URL: https://example.com/standard-terms
#    Body:
#      "Commercial Use of this Work requires a separate written
#       agreement with the Maintainer. Email [email protected] with
#       a description of your intended use. We respond within 14 days.
#       No public pricing; each use case is negotiated individually."
#
# 5. TIERED PRICING (public schedule, multiple bands)
#    URL: https://example.com/standard-terms
#    Body:
#      "Commercial Use of this Work requires payment per the following
#       schedule (annual, paid in advance):
#         ARR under $100K:      $500/year flat
#         ARR $100K – $1M:      0.5% of ARR
#         ARR $1M – $10M:       0.25% of ARR
#         ARR over $10M:        0.1% of ARR
#       ARR = Annual Recurring Revenue attributable to the Derivative.
#       Payment address: bank wire on request, or Stripe at
#       https://buy.stripe.com/example-link."
